  },
  "description": "ERACEG crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P 21 21 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C77 H97 Dy3 Mn6 N6 O37 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.340-3.973 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.05-109.05°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy3Mn6(L)6(μ2-OMe)6(OAc)(H2O)2(HOMe)3](NO3)2·6H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Dy(III), Mn(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
